    <string name="pref_openweather_api_key_title">OpenWeather API key</string>
    <string name="pref_apply_api_title">Apply for API</string>
    <string name="pref_weather_api_guide_intro">OpenWeather API key setup and configuration guide.</string>
    <string name="pref_weather_api_guide_prepare">Step 1: Preparation\n- An email address that can receive verification messages\n- A network environment that can reach the OpenWeather website</string>
    <string name="pref_weather_api_guide_step_register1">Step 2: Register an OpenWeather account\n1. Open https://openweathermap.org/ and tap the orange Login button at the top right (see image 1).</string>
    <string name="pref_weather_api_guide_step_register2">2. On the sign-in page, tap Create an Account.</string>
    <string name="pref_weather_api_guide_step_register3">3. Fill the registration form (see image 3):\n    Username: custom name for account identification\n    Enter email: your valid email address for verification and account recovery\n    Password: set your password\n    Repeat password: enter the same password again\nSubmit the form to register.</string>
    <string name="pref_weather_api_guide_step_verify1">Step 3: Verify your email\n1. After registration, the page shows: We have sent the confirmation link to xxx@xx.com. Please check your email. 2. Open your email, find the message from OpenWeather, and tap the Verify your email button to complete verification. (see image 5)\nIf you do not receive the email, check spam or promotions folders.</string>
    <string name="pref_weather_api_guide_step_verify2">2. Open your email, find the message from OpenWeather, and tap the Verify your email button to complete verification.</string>
    <string name="pref_weather_api_guide_step_verify3">If you do not receive the email, check spam or promotions folders.</string>
    <string name="pref_weather_api_guide_step_key1">Step 4: Get your API key\n1. After verification, return to OpenWeather and sign in.\n2. In your account dashboard, open API Keys from the navigation menu.</string>
    <string name="pref_weather_api_guide_step_key2">3. On the API management page, copy the default generated key (usually named Default, status Active), or enter a name and tap Generate to create a new key.</string>
    <string name="pref_weather_api_guide_step_key3">Important: free keys are limited to 60 calls per minute and 1000 per day, which is enough for personal wallpaper use. Do not share your key publicly to avoid misuse and account throttling.</string>
    <string name="pref_weather_api_guide_step_config1">Step 5: Configure the API key in the wallpaper app\n1. Open the wallpaper app and tap the cloud icon at the top right.</string>
    <string name="pref_weather_api_guide_step_config2">2. Select OpenWeather API key from the popup menu.</string>
    <string name="pref_weather_api_guide_step_config3">3. Paste the copied API key into the input box and tap Confirm to save.</string>
    <string name="pref_weather_api_guide_step_config4">4. Tap Refresh Weather Now to test. If the wallpaper loads weather information normally, the configuration is successful.</string>
    <string name="pref_weather_api_guide_common">Step 6: Troubleshooting\n- Verify the key is copied completely without extra spaces or line breaks.\n- A new API key may take 10–30 minutes to activate; wait and try again.\n- Make sure location permission is enabled in the app.</string>
